`0result.sql` incorrectly counts variants because it joins to `alternate_bases` and uses `COUNT(*)`, which would over‑count if any row carries more than one alternate allele (it only happens to give 5 604 here by chance).  
`2result.sql` under‑counts variants (5 264 instead of 5 604) and therefore reports a wrong total number of alleles.  
`1result.sql` derives the variant count directly from the base table (no risk of double‑counting), uses the correct sums for AC and AN, and lists the distinct gene symbols correctly. Hence it is the only robust and correct solution.

```plaintext
1result.sql
```